# Repository hygiene

- Do not add AI/process files (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `PROMPT.md`, diaries, prompt transcripts).
- Do not mention Cursor, ChatGPT, or AI generation in public pages or README.
- Comments only for non-obvious, accessibility-sensitive, or deployment-sensitive behavior.
- Keep README and docs short and useful to future officers.
- Preserve MIT attribution and license text.
- Do not invent officers, emails, events, partners, dues, or other chapter facts.
- Prefer simple, maintainable code. Do not add dependencies without a clear need.
- No demo/sample content, dead scaffolding, or unused placeholders.
- Do not copy research dumps into the repository.
